(Neural Network Utility Approximation Agent)
Overview

This module demonstrates a from-scratch neural network + training pipeline used to approximate a hand-designed game-state evaluation function. The end result is a deployed agent that can evaluate states using a compact feed-forward neural network instead of calling the original heuristic directly.

This is a practical example of supervised learning for value-function approximation (common in reinforcement learning and game AI systems), including:

feature engineering + normalization

data logging from live gameplay

offline training + weight export

inference-only deployment inside an agent loop

Files
NeuralNetworks.py

A compact two-layer sigmoid neural network implementation (4 inputs → 8 hidden → 1 output) trained on a fixed truth table dataset.

Purpose:

Validates backpropagation and convergence behavior

Produces a working NN implementation with stable training output

Key traits:

sigmoid activations

stochastic training updates per epoch

prints only the training error during learning (useful for grading + debugging)

trainingNN_helper.py

Offline trainer used to learn weights from real gameplay logs.

What it does:

reads train_log.csv (features + target utility labels)

trains a small 2-layer sigmoid network using NumPy

prints learned weights in pasteable Python-list format for deployment

This is your “training pipeline” script—run it once you have enough logged samples.

MinDiffNN.py

Deployed agent that uses a trained neural network as its evaluation function.

What it does:

maps a game state into 5 normalized input features

runs feed-forward inference using frozen weights (W1, b1, W2, b2)

uses that predicted utility to score 1-ply lookahead nodes

includes an optional logging mode to generate new training data

Important switches:

USE_NN = True → evaluation uses the trained NN

LOGGING_ENABLED = True → writes feature/label rows into train_log.csv

How the System Works (Pipeline)

Teacher signal (heuristic utility)

MinDiffNN.py contains a hand-written utility(state) function that outputs a score in [0, 1].

Feature extraction

map_state_to_features(state) compresses the state into a small normalized vector (5 features).

Data logging

When LOGGING_ENABLED = True, each state produces a row:

[features..., heuristic_utility] → train_log.csv

Offline training

trainingNN_helper.py trains on that CSV and prints learned weights.

Deployment

Paste the trained weights into MinDiffNN.py.

With USE_NN = True, the agent evaluates states using NN inference only.

This mirrors real ML workflows: collect → train → deploy.

Running / Usage Notes

To generate training data:

set LOGGING_ENABLED = True in MinDiffNN.py

run games to populate train_log.csv

To train weights:

run trainingNN_helper.py

paste the printed weights into MinDiffNN.py

To deploy inference-only:

set USE_NN = True

set LOGGING_ENABLED = False

Why This Matters (Employer Context)

This module demonstrates applied ML engineering skills:

building and training a neural network (forward + backprop)

feature scaling and compact state representations

offline training and reproducible inference deployment

integrating ML inference into a real-time decision loop

